\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, my soul, thy suit prepare,
\par Jesus loves to answer prayer;
\par He Himself has bid Thee pray,
\par Therefore will not say thee nay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou art coming to a King;
\par Large petitions with thee bring;
\par For His grace and power are such,
\par None can ever ask too much.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. With my burden I begin:
\par Lord, remove this load of sin;
\par Let Thy blood, for sinners spilt,
\par Set my concience free from guilt.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, I come to Thee for rest;
\par Take possession of my breast;
\par There Thy blood-bought right maintain,
\par And without a rival reign.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. While I am a pilgrim here,
\par Let Thy love my spirit cheer:
\par As my Guide, my Guard, my Friend,
\par Lead me to my journey's end.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

